Any matrix $matbold(M)$ decomposes as $matbold(M) = matbold(S) + matbold(A)$ with $matbold(S)$ symmetric and $matbold(A)$ antisymmetric. Since $bold(x)^tp matbold(A) bold(x) = 0$ for antisymmetric $matbold(A)$ and all $bold(x) in RR^n$,

$ bold(x)^tp matbold(M) bold(x) = bold(x)^tp matbold(S) bold(x), $

which is why only symmetric matrices need appear in the definition of quadratic forms.
